<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Architecture for Independently Pretrained Models Setting</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conducted additional experiments using a DenseNet-121 as the old model, <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\text{old}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\text{old}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and an EfficientNet-B3 as the new model, <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\text{new}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>new</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\text{new}}</annotation></semantics></math>, both pretrained on ImageNet1K and obtained from the PyTorch Hub. The results of these experiments on the ImageNet1K dataset are presented in Table <a href="#A2.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Appendix B Additional Architecture for Independently Pretrained Models Setting ‣ 𝝀-Orthogonality Regularization for Compatible Representation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. Our approach achieves the best performance across all metrics, outperforming the baselines in both cross-model and same-model retrieval scenarios.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 6</span>: </span><span id="A2.T6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Compatibility results on ImageNet1K under the Independently Pretrained Models setting. We use two independently trained models: DenseNet-121 as the old model, <math id="A2.T6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\text{old}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\text{old}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and an EfficientNet-B3 as the new model, <math id="A2.T6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\text{new}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>new</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\text{new}}</annotation></semantics></math>, both pretrained on ImageNet1K and obtained from the PyTorch Hub.</span></figcaption>
