<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A6.T11.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 11</span>: </span><span id="A6.T11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">CMC-Top1 (%) on CUB for different loss combinations (<math id="A6.T11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\checkmark" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>✓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\checkmark</annotation></semantics></math> = included, <math id="A6.T11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> = excluded). The setting is the same of Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.1 Image Retrieval Compatibility ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ 𝝀-Orthogonality Regularization for Compatible Representation Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, where the first model, <math id="A6.T11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\text{old}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\text{old}}</annotation></semantics></math>, is a ResNet-18, whereas the second, <math id="A6.T11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\text{new}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>new</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\text{new}}</annotation></semantics></math>, is a ViT-L-16. A backward adapter <math id="A6.T11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.T11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=12</annotation></semantics></math> is used to adapt the improved model on the downstream task.</span></figcaption>
