</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="A6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To further validate our aproach we also study the effect of a scalar weight <math id="A6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> to the loss contributions of our <math id="A6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>-orthogonal regularization compared with two different orthogonal regularization Soft Orthogonality (SO)<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>—witch correspond to the spacial case of <math id="A6.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> =0 in our aproach— and Spectral Restricted Isometry Property (SRIP)<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>. We tested the regularizers with values <math id="A6.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=10^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=10^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=10^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=10^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>. Additionally, we include a column reporting the exact value of <math id="A6.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert W^{\top}W-I\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert W^{\top}W-I\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> reached by the backward transformation <math id="A6.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> at the end of training, to indicate the deviation from strict orthogonality.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.T12" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A6.T12.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 12</span>: </span><span id="A6.T12.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of orthogonal regularization methods with different weight scales <math id="A6.T12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>.
Compatibility metrics on the downstream task CUB200 and zero-shot (ZS) CMC-Top1 gain on ImageNet1K.
Parentheses show the increment in CMC-Top1 over the independently trained new model.
The last column reports the final value of <math id="A6.T12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert W^{\top}W-I\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" mathsize="1.110em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" mathsize="1.110em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert W^{\top}W-I\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
